course: dictionary
lesson: 3235
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning to use. The word entry is a good example. Its meaning depends on where you find it, like a door, a diary, or a competition.
explain: Look for clues. «Last entry is at 5:15» tells you entry means the time you are allowed to go in. «A diary entry is written in the first person» tells you entry means a piece of writing in a diary. Ask yourself: is this about going in, writing, or sending something in?
explain: Always test your meaning by putting it in the sentence in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right. If it does not, try another meaning from the list.
fact: Entry is a noun. Its plural is entries.
fact: Entry can mean a way in, like a door or gate, or the act of going in.
fact: Entry can mean a piece written in a diary, dictionary, list or log.
fact: Entry can mean something you send into a competition, or the permission to go in.
fact: The context tells you which meaning is right: «No entry» on a gate means you may not go in.
exercise: «Many places have a last entry time before closing time.» What does entry mean here? | *The time by which you are allowed to go in | Something you send into a contest | A page in a diary | A piece of writing in a list
exercise: «Her entry for the painting contest arrived on time.» What is her entry? | A gate at the back of the park | A word meaning quiet | *Her painting, sent in to the competition | A page in her diary about the day
exercise: «Ella wrote a diary entry about her first day at the new school.» What kind of text is a diary entry? | A sign on a door | A fee paid to join a club | *A written piece in a diary | A ticket for a train
test: A sign on a gate says «No entry». What does it mean? | Leave your bag at the gate | You may go in if you ask nicely | *You are not allowed to go in | Pay a fee at the gate
test: «The entry fee for the museum is five pounds.» What is an entry fee? | Money you win in a contest | *Money you pay to go in | A list of the museum rooms | A page in a visitor's diary
exam: «She filled in the entry form for the spelling bee.» What is an entry form? | *A form to send in to a competition | A form giving permission to leave early | A written note in her diary | A gate at the back of the school
